   "source": [
    "## 7.4 Summary\n",
    "- In the world of Large Language Models (LLMs), agents refer to software entities designed to perform tasks autonomously or semi-autonomously using the capabilities of the LLM.\n",
    "- Tools are interfaces that an agent can use to interact with.\n",
    "- LangChain Agents use language models to interact with other tools and are designed to perform well-designed tasks.\n",
    "- The Python Agent is an agent which executes LLM-generated Python code.\n",
    "- The Pandas DataFrame Agent is designed to facilitate the interaction of a Pandas Dataframe with LLMs.\n",
    "the CSV Agent allows you to simply specify the CSV filename, and will automatically load it as a Pandas DataFrame behind the scenes using the Pandas DataFrame Agent.\n",
    "- The JSON Agent allows you to work with a JSON file and ask queries.\n",
    "- The CodeAgent generates code to solve the task and then executes the code.\n",
    "- The ReactCodeAgent solves the problem step by step, and writes the tool call in Python.\n",
    "- The ReactJsonAgent solves the problem step by step, and writes the tool call in JSON."
   ]
  },
